# Chroma library, modern Earth: what the care sphere's events bring into a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22"
# update stage 4, item 15 phase 3: a moment for each modern event that touches the character). Design:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data: chroma-ideas/spheres-data/care.json
# (events[].on_character and wording.modern). Fields: build.py (WORLD_SIT, WORLD_OPT, the spheres' fields).
#
# Every moment here is one a sphere event brings: per_year is all 0 (they exist only with the spheres' events on, switch
# sph_events), there are no drivers, and the Engine fires each on its event for the people its selector names. The
# '# world:' line above each names the event key, the selector and the share of selected people who get the moment
# (estimate). Each carries sphere: care and sphere_event: <key>; every option carries the face it acts in (one-colour
# option X: care.X; pair option: the pair face in wheel order, so "- WR" takes care.RW).
#
# Care's modern events with an on_character line are 19. Three are left out because a moment in earth.py already is
# the same thing: plague_wave and quarantine (the world's pandemic, which closes the town: the read event 'a pandemic
# and a lockdown' in earth-events.lib), and remedy_works (the life event 'a cure is found at last' in
# earth-world-eras.lib, which the Engine fires when medical capability passes a disease). neglect_scandal is kept: the
# world's C3 cover-up has a moment only for the staff who know ('the thing the bosses are hiding'); this one is for the
# families of the residents when the scandal breaks.
#
# Layout: seventeen moments, each a life event with even alpha, the five one-colour options plus one half of a pair set.
# Twelve use both halves of D1 to D6 once (every pair 6 times), four use both halves of D1 and D2 again, and the
# seventeenth uses D3b, so the pairs of D3b (BR UG UR WB WG) appear 9 times and the rest 8.
# Evenness: in every moment each colour's one-colour chance plus half its two pairs' chances is the same sum, so every
# colour has the same mean chance in each moment and so in every stage. No flags.
# Tone from the event: good = joy, bad = trouble, mixed = mixed (seven joy, four trouble, six mixed).
# Illness is told plainly and kindly; nothing graphic; no harm to a child (a hard birth ends with mother and baby safe).
# Syntax: header of build.py.
#
# share: on every moment (2026-10-10, Engine phase 3a) is its '# world:' share: the engine draws at birth who can
# ever meet it, so when the event comes to town only that share of the people there are open to the moment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- neighbours_rush (good; pairs D1a)

# world: sphere event neighbours_rush, selector place, share .4
== the street pulls together after the storm
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 5-20
times: World event: neighbours_rush (sphere care). It follows the town's flood, fire or storm (prot.disaster_strikes) where help from the council is slow or far; about 4 in 10 residents are drawn into the helping (share .4, estimate), so once or twice in a life in a place that floods or storms (estimate)
likelier: a street where people know each other, old neighbours who live alone, a car or a generator, help from the council far away
rarer: a block where nobody knows anyone, a part of town the storm spared
tone: joy
life: community, home
horizon: week
roles: elder, friend, neighbours
who: neighbour
sphere: care
sphere_event: neighbours_rush
share: .4
earth: the storm cuts the power, and the street checks on the old, shares a generator and drives the sick to the clinic
scene: The storm takes the power out across {place} at dusk, and the phones go soon after. {elder}, two doors down, lives alone with a breathing machine that needs to be plugged in. Up and down the street, torches are coming on.
scene W: Someone has to know who on the street is old, alone or ill, and make sure no door is missed. {N} reaches for a pen.
scene U: {N} works out what is needed first: power for the breathing machine, a road to the clinic, and who has a full tank.
scene B: {N} has the only generator on the street and a full can of fuel. Tonight that makes {N} the most useful person for a mile.
scene R: {N} is already pulling on boots, torch in hand, before anyone has asked.
scene G: The old ones remember the last big storm, when the whole street ate together for a week. {N} puts the big pot on the gas.
- W | go door to door with a list, and tick off every house that answers | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: care.W | chance: 72
- U | find out who needs power for a machine, and plan whose turn the generator is | v: benevolence, achievement | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | run your generator for the old neighbour, and ask the street to chip in for fuel | v: benevolence, power | sphere: care.B | chance: 77
- R | drive the old neighbour to the clinic before the low road floods | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | cook for the whole street on the gas ring, and keep the kettle going all night | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: made a friend | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- BG | open your house as the warm room for anyone without heat tonight | v: benevolence, security | sphere: care.BG | chance: 66
- BR | run a cable from your generator to three houses, though it is not allowed | v: benevolence, stimulation | lever: subvert | sphere: care.BR | chance: 60
- UG | check each old neighbour's pills, and make sure nobody runs out before the roads open | v: benevolence, security | sphere: care.GU | chance: 64
- WR | join the crew clearing the fallen tree from the road to the clinic | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: care.RW | chance: 70
- WU | pin a list on the noticeboard of who needs what and who can give it | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: care.WU | chance: 66
works: By morning every door on the street has been knocked on, and nobody spent the night alone.
works: Years later the street still waves to each other, because of that night.
fails: The night is long and cold, and {N} ends it soaked, worn out and unsure the help went where it was needed most.
fails: Two neighbours fall out over the generator, and the street remembers that more than the rest.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cure_fails (bad; pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event cure_fails, selector place, share .05
== a medicine in the cupboard is withdrawn
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: cure_fails (sphere care). A widely used medicine is withdrawn for a harm found late a few times in a long life (estimate); it reaches the person through a parent who took it, about 1 in 20 people where it was prescribed widely (share .05, estimate)
likelier: a parent with a long illness, a new medicine given widely and fast, a place with weak checks before a medicine is sold
rarer: careful prescribing, strong licensing and long trials
tone: trouble
life: health, family
horizon: months
roles: parent, sibling
who: parent
sphere: care
sphere_event: cure_fails
share: .05
earth: a new pill a parent of yours has taken for a year is linked to heart attacks and withdrawn
scene: The news says the new pill for sore joints, approved in a hurry, is being withdrawn: it has been linked to heart attacks. {parent} has taken one every morning for a year, and rings {N} that evening, frightened.
scene W: Someone signed that pill off without enough checks. {N} wants to know who, and wants it set down properly.
scene U: {N} looks up the study that sank the pill: how many took it, how many were harmed, and what the risk is for {parent} now.
scene B: There will be a claim, and lawyers are already advertising for it. {N} means to see {parent} counted and paid.
scene R: {parent} trusted that doctor completely. {N} is shaking with anger.
scene G: {N} thinks there must be gentler ways to live with sore joints, and that {parent} needs company more than another new pill.
- W | write a formal complaint to the health board, with the dates and the prescription | v: conformity, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: institution hospital | sphere: care.W | chance: 73
- U | book your parent a heart check, and go through the study with the doctor | v: security, self-direction | sphere: care.U | chance: 71
- B | sign your parent up to the group claim against the pill's maker | v: power, security | lever: voice | pushes: economy | sphere: care.B | chance: 69
- R | go to the surgery and tell the doctor who prescribed it exactly what you think | v: stimulation, universalism | mark: made an enemy | lever: voice | pushes: institution hospital | sphere: care.R | chance: 76
- G | spend the next weeks at your parent's side, and keep the house calm | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 72
- RG | take your parent off the new pills and onto walks, rest and good food | v: benevolence, hedonism | lever: exit | sphere: care.RG | chance: 60
- UB | find a specialist of your own choosing for a second opinion | v: self-direction, security | lever: exit | sphere: care.UB | chance: 70
- UR | get the other patients talking online, and push the maker for the full data | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: economy | sphere: care.UR | chance: 54
- WB | press the health board to pay for heart checks for everyone who took it | v: universalism, power | lever: voice | pushes: institution hospital | sphere: care.WB | chance: 58
- WG | start a support group for the families of people who took the pill | v: benevolence, universalism | lever: found | sphere: care.GW | chance: 62
works: {parent}'s heart check comes back clear, and the worry in the house finally lifts.
works: The maker settles, the rules for new medicines tighten, and {N} had a small hand in it.
fails: The complaint goes into a long queue and comes back months later with a form letter.
fails: {parent} stops trusting any doctor at all, and the next real illness is left too long.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- remedy_feared (mixed; pairs D2a)

# world: sphere event remedy_feared, selector place, share .3
== the new vaccine splits the dinner table
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 8-25
times: World event: remedy_feared (sphere care). A new vaccine meets a rumour that spreads faster than the facts a few times in a life (estimate); the quarrel reaches about 3 in 10 people in the place through family or friends (share .3, estimate)
likelier: a family with members on both sides, distrust of officials, a rumour a famous name repeats, an old or frail relative
rarer: a family that trusts its doctor, a quiet year with nothing new offered
tone: mixed
life: family, health
horizon: months
roles: sibling, parent
who: sibling
sphere: care
sphere_event: remedy_feared
share: .3
earth: a rumour about the new vaccine spreads faster than the virus, and a family dinner ends in silence
scene: The new vaccine is offered to everyone, and a rumour about it is spreading faster than the illness. At Sunday dinner {sibling} says nobody in the family should touch it, and the table goes silent.
scene W: The health board has asked everyone to take it, so that the old and the sick are kept safe. {N} thinks that is what a neighbour does.
scene U: {N} has read the rumour and the studies side by side, and only one of them shows its numbers.
scene B: Nobody is going to tell {N} what goes into {Ns} own body, not the board and not {sibling}. {N} will weigh it alone.
scene R: {N} can feel the argument coming like a storm, and is half ready to start it.
scene G: The family has eaten together every Sunday for twenty years. {N} cares more about that table than about who is right.
- W | book the vaccine for yourself, and help the old neighbours book theirs | v: universalism, conformity | tech: modern medicine | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | send your sibling the study, with the numbers marked, and ask them to read it | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: care.U | chance: 52
- B | ask your own doctor about your own case, and decide in your own time | v: self-direction | sphere: care.B | chance: 66
- R | tell your sibling across the table that the rumour is dangerous nonsense | v: stimulation, universalism | mark: made an enemy | sphere: care.R | chance: 59
- G | change the subject, pass the potatoes, and keep the family at one table | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: care.G | chance: 80
- BG | wait and see how it goes for others before deciding anything | v: security | sphere: care.BG | chance: 70
- BR | refuse it out loud, and say your body is your own business | v: self-direction | mark: defied an authority | sphere: care.BR | chance: 66
- UR | take it on the first day, and tell everyone honestly how it went | v: stimulation, universalism | sphere: care.UR | chance: 84
- WG | ask the family doctor round to answer everyone's questions over tea | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: care.GW | chance: 38
- WU | volunteer at the vaccine clinic, checking names and answering questions | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: care.WU | chance: 80
works: The argument cools, and by summer the family is back at one table, whatever each one chose.
works: {N} makes the choice with a clear head, and keeps the respect of the people who chose otherwise.
fails: {sibling} stops coming on Sundays, and the empty chair stays empty all year.
fails: Whatever {N} decides, half the family takes it as an insult, and says so for months.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- birth_safer (good; pairs D2b)

# world: sphere event birth_safer, selector place, share .1
== a new birth centre in town
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-65
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 15-40
times: World event: birth_safer (sphere care). A town gains a new maternity unit or birth centre perhaps once in a generation (estimate); it reaches the person when a brother or sister is expecting as it opens, about 1 in 10 residents (share .1, estimate)
likelier: a young family, a sibling expecting, a growing town
rarer: nobody in the family expecting, a remote place the new unit does not reach
tone: joy
life: family, health
horizon: months
roles: sibling, parent, partner
who: sibling
at: hospital
sphere: care
sphere_event: birth_safer
share: .1
earth: the new maternity unit opens with a midwife-led birth centre beside it, just as your brother's or sister's baby is due
scene: The new maternity unit has opened in {place}, with a birth centre run by midwives beside it. {sibling} and their partner are expecting their first baby next month, and the whole family has an opinion on where it should be born.
scene W: There are leaflets for both, with checklists and visiting hours. {N} wants {sibling} to have the safest care going, and every box ticked.
scene U: {N} looks up the figures for both: how often mothers are moved across for help, and how far the theatre is from the birth rooms.
scene B: It is {sibling}'s baby and {sibling}'s choice, and {N} means to make sure the family respects it.
scene R: {N} has already offered to be the one who drives them in, at any hour, in any weather.
scene G: Every baby in the family for three generations was born with the same old midwife. {N} wonders what the new place will feel like.
- W | go with your sibling to the open evening, and ask about every safety check | v: security, benevolence | sphere: care.W | chance: 80
- U | read the figures for both places, and lay them out plainly for the family | v: self-direction, benevolence | sphere: care.U | chance: 76
- B | tell the family the choice belongs to the parents, and make them stop arguing | v: self-direction | sphere: care.B | chance: 74
- R | promise to be on call day and night for the dash to the hospital | v: benevolence, stimulation | mark: kept your word | sphere: care.R | chance: 82
- G | cook and freeze meals for the weeks after the birth | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 81
- RG | learn the breathing and the back rubs, in case you are the one beside them | v: benevolence | mark: learned a skill | sphere: care.RG | chance: 76
- UB | help them write a birth plan of their own, with every choice spelled out | v: self-direction, security | sphere: care.UB | chance: 86
- UG | sit in on a midwives' class and learn what the first weeks really need | v: benevolence, self-direction | sphere: care.GU | chance: 76
- WB | give to the new unit's appeal, and see the family's name on the donors' board | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | pushes: institution hospital | sphere: care.WB | chance: 80
- WR | sign up as a volunteer driver, taking families to the birth centre at night | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: care.RW | chance: 74
works: The baby arrives at the new centre on a calm night, and the new family is home within two days.
works: The new place does its work well, and {N} becomes the relative every new parent in the family calls first.
fails: The family argument outlasts the birth, and {sibling} remembers who said what.
fails: The birth goes well, but {Ns} help is barely needed, and {N} feels oddly left out.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hard_birth (mixed; pairs D3a)

# world: sphere event hard_birth, selector members (the household where the birth is), share .5
== the labour that stalls in the night
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-60
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 2-10
times: World event: hard_birth (sphere care). A long or stalled labour that needs the surgical team comes in perhaps 1 birth in 8 in a modern hospital (estimate); the moment goes to the partner who waits through it (share .5 of the household, estimate). With a modern team close by, mother and baby come through
likelier: a first baby, a long way to the hospital, a baby lying the wrong way
rarer: a second or later birth, a hospital close by with skilled hands
tone: mixed
life: family, health, children
horizon: moment
roles: partner, parent
who: partner
at: hospital
sphere: care
sphere_event: hard_birth
share: .5
earth: your partner's labour stalls in the night, the midwife calls the surgical team, and within the hour mother and baby are safe
scene: Eighteen hours in, {partner}'s labour has stalled. The midwife presses the call button, the room fills with calm people in scrubs, and there will be an operation within the hour. {N} is handed a gown and told to wait.
scene W: The team has a procedure for this, and they follow it step by step. {N} holds on to that.
scene U: {N} asks the midwife exactly what is happening and what happens next, and listens to every word.
scene B: {N} wants the senior doctor, not the junior one, and wants to be in that room.
scene R: Every part of {N} wants to do something, anything, and there is nothing to do but wait.
scene G: {N} holds {partner}'s hand and keeps breathing slowly with them, as if the two of them could slow the clock.
- W | do exactly as the staff ask, and keep out of their way | v: conformity, security | sphere: care.W | chance: 81
- U | ask the midwife to explain each step, and pass it on plainly to the family | v: security, benevolence | sphere: care.U | chance: 76
- B | ask for the senior surgeon by name, and ask to be beside your partner in theatre | v: power, security | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | talk and joke with your partner all the way to theatre, to keep the fear away | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: care.R | chance: 82
- G | hold your partner's hand and breathe with them, slow and steady | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 76
- BG | tell both families plainly what is happening, and ask them to wait at home | v: security, benevolence | sphere: care.BG | chance: 80
- RG | rub your partner's back through each wave of pain until the team arrives | v: benevolence | sphere: care.RG | chance: 76
- UB | read the consent form line by line, and ask what each risk really means | v: self-direction, security | sphere: care.UB | chance: 78
- WR | run for the midwife the moment the monitor changes | v: benevolence, security | sphere: care.RW | chance: 68
- WU | write down every time and every word the doctors say, for later | v: security, conformity | sphere: care.WU | chance: 78
works: Within the hour {partner} and the baby are safe, and {N} is holding someone very small and very loud.
works: The night is long and frightening, and by dawn the three of them are together and well.
fails: {partner} and the baby come through well, but {N} cannot shake the fear of that night for months.
fails: Everyone is safe, yet {N} keeps going over every minute of it, wishing they had done more.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- good_death (good; pairs D3b)

# world: sphere event good_death, selector place, share .05
== the hospice nurse comes every morning
tier: life event
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-40
times: World event: good_death (sphere care). Where a hospice service reaches the town, it touches those with a parent in their last months, about 1 in 20 adults there (share .05, estimate); in rich countries many who die of a long illness now have some hospice care at the end (estimate). The parent's death itself is the moment 'a parent dies'
likelier: a parent with a long illness, a hospice service nearby, a family that lives close
rarer: a sudden death, no hospice within reach, a family scattered far
tone: joy
life: family, death
horizon: months
roles: parent, sibling, partner
who: parent
sphere: care
sphere_event: good_death
share: .05
earth: the hospice nurse comes every day, and your parent dies at home, in their own bed, without pain
scene: The treatments have stopped, and the hospice nurse comes to {parent}'s house every morning now. There is no pain, the bed is by the window, and the days that are left are quiet ones.
scene W: The nurse has drawn up a rota for the family, and {N} means to keep to it, so {parent} is never left alone.
scene U: {N} asks the nurse plainly what the last days will look like, and is glad of a plain answer.
scene B: {parent} has always run their own life. {N} means to see that they choose how the end goes too.
scene R: {N} wants to fill every day with something {parent} loves: the old songs, the dog, the view from the hill.
scene G: The family sits with {parent} the way {parent} once sat with their own parents: no fuss, just there.
- W | keep the family rota, so someone is with your parent day and night | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: loyalty | sphere: care.W | chance: 81
- U | ask the nurse plainly what the last days will bring, and tell the family | v: benevolence, security | sphere: care.U | chance: 82
- B | help your parent write down their own wishes for the end, and see them kept | v: self-direction, benevolence | sphere: care.B | chance: 77
- R | bring in the old friends, the music and the stories for one last good evening | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: care.R | chance: 78
- G | sit by the bed in the evenings and simply hold their hand | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 83
- BR | pour your parent the glass of whisky they ask for, whatever the leaflet says | v: hedonism, self-direction | sphere: care.BR | chance: 86
- UG | learn from the nurse how to ease a dry mouth and turn the pillows yourself | v: benevolence | mark: learned a skill | sphere: care.GU | chance: 78
- UR | set up a video call, so the cousins far away can say goodbye | v: benevolence, stimulation | tech: video calls | sphere: care.UR | chance: 80
- WB | give to the hospice that cares for your parent, and join its circle of friends | v: benevolence, universalism | lever: fund | sphere: care.WB | chance: 82
- WG | share the nights with your siblings, so that no one wears out | v: benevolence | lever: loyalty | sphere: care.GW | chance: 78
works: {parent} dies at home in their own bed, without pain, with family in the room.
works: The grief, when it comes, is heavy but clean, and {N} is glad of every evening spent.
fails: The last weeks are peaceful, but {N} spends too many of them on the phone and the forms, and regrets it.
fails: An old quarrel between the siblings flares by the bedside, and lingers past the funeral.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- house_of_care_opens (good; pairs D4a)

# world: sphere event house_of_care_opens, selector place, share .4
== a clinic opens on the corner
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 16-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: house_of_care_opens (sphere care). A new clinic or health centre opens in a neighbourhood perhaps once in twenty years (estimate); about 4 in 10 residents notice it in their own lives, as patients or as staff (share .4, estimate)
likelier: a neighbourhood that has gone without, a council or charity with funds, a sickness just past
rarer: a place already well served, a remote village
tone: joy
life: health, community, work
horizon: months
roles: parent, friend
at: hospital
sphere: care
sphere_event: house_of_care_opens
share: .4
earth: a clinic opens in your neighbourhood: a doctor, two nurses, and evening hours that fit working people
scene: A clinic has opened on the corner where the old bank used to be: a doctor, two nurses and evening hours that fit working people. There is a notice in the window asking for volunteers and a part-time receptionist.
scene W: At last, care that anyone on the street can walk into, waiting their turn like everyone else.
scene U: {N} has put off a check-up for two years. Now there is no excuse, and {N} is curious what it will find.
scene B: A new clinic needs staff, and the part-time post would fit around {Ns} other work very neatly.
scene R: {N} walks in on the opening day just to see it, and ends up helping carry in the chairs.
scene G: {parent} has never trusted the big hospital across town. A clinic two streets away, with a nurse who knows the family, might be different.
- W | register the whole family at the clinic, and book everyone's check-ups | v: security, benevolence | sphere: care.W | chance: 81
- U | book the blood tests you have put off for two years | v: security | sphere: care.U | chance: 89
- B | apply for the part-time post on the desk, on hours that suit you | v: achievement, security | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | volunteer on the opening day, and stay on for the evening rush | v: benevolence, stimulation | mark: made a friend | sphere: care.R | chance: 85
- G | take your parent along, and introduce them to the nurse yourself | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.G | chance: 78
- BG | tell your parent plainly that the cough needs looking at, and walk them in | v: benevolence | sphere: care.BG | chance: 82
- RG | join the clinic's walking group on Saturday mornings | v: hedonism, security | sphere: care.RG | chance: 78
- UR | offer to set up the clinic's online booking yourself, over a weekend | v: achievement, stimulation | tech: internet | sphere: care.UR | chance: 68
- WB | give to the appeal for the clinic's new wing, and see your name on the board | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | pushes: institution hospital | sphere: care.WB | chance: 84
- WU | join the patients' group that checks the clinic keeps its promises | v: universalism, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: institution hospital | sphere: care.WU | chance: 70
works: The clinic becomes part of the street, and {N} and the family are known there by name.
works: A check-up there catches something small before it grows, and the whole family is grateful.
fails: Within a year the evening hours are cut, and the waiting room is as full as the old one.
fails: {N} means to go and never quite does, and the leaflet sits on the fridge all winter.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- water_clean (good; pairs D4b)

# world: sphere event water_clean, selector place, share .5
== the tap water is safe again
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-100
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 20-60
times: World event: water_clean (sphere care). A town rebuilds its waterworks after a fouling or a long run of warnings perhaps once in a long life (estimate); about half of residents feel it in daily life (share .5, estimate)
likelier: a town that had a water scandal or boil-water warnings, a family with small children or someone frail
rarer: a town whose water was always clean, a home on its own well
tone: joy
life: home, health, community
horizon: months
roles: parent, friend, neighbours
at: council
sphere: care
sphere_event: water_clean
share: .5
earth: the water plant is rebuilt after the scandal, and for the first time in years people drink from the tap
scene: The new water plant is open, the boil-water notices are coming down, and the council says the tap is safe. In {Ns} kitchen there are still three crates of bottled water by the door.
scene W: The council did it properly in the end: tested, signed off, published. {N} trusts a job done by the rules.
scene U: {N} wants to see the test results before anyone in the house drinks a glass.
scene B: {N} has spent a small fortune on bottled water. Now that money is {Ns} own again.
scene R: {N} fills a pint glass straight from the tap and drinks it down in one go.
